    description: "## Origin\n\nSplit out of **WI-sitos** (the WI-sozoj residual) on owner direction\n(2026-07-16): SQLAlchemy is the one piece of that residual that does NOT land on\nthe current DEEP cohort (pretix is Django, not SQLAlchemy), so it is broader\nfuture work rather than terminal-wave (Wave-5) cohort completion. Deliberately\n**untagged `wave5`** — pick it up when a SQLAlchemy repo enters a cohort or the\nio-boundary receiver-inference thread is being generalized.\n\n## Scope\n\nMake SQLAlchemy ORM/Core database I/O visible to the io-boundary detector via\nthe same type-verified receiver-typing shape WI-sozoj shipped for Django\n(PR #695, dev 5dcfad4927):\n\n- **ORM session:** `Session.query`/`add`/`delete`/`commit`/`flush`/`execute`,\n  `scoped_session` proxies. Type the receiver via the external base\n  (`sqlalchemy.orm.Session`) and emit a `sqlalchemy.orm`-module-qualified\n  `calls` edge, then a type-verified python.yaml carve-out classifies\n  read/write (query/get → db_read; add/delete/commit/flush → db_write).\n- **Core engine:** `Engine.execute`, `Connection.execute` — external-base\n  receiver typing on `sqlalchemy.engine.*`.\n- **Declarative models:** a class extending `declarative_base()` /\n  `DeclarativeBase` is the Model analogue for instance writes\n  (`obj` added/deleted through a Session, not a `.save()` method — SQLAlchemy\n  has no instance `.save()`, so the write surface is Session-mediated).\n\n## Method (reuse WI-sozoj's shape)\n\nThe exact producer/consumer division WI-sozoj established: py.py types the\nreceiver (framework-syntax marker / external base) → module-qualified dst →\npython.yaml type-verified carve-out classifies (module-filter path, never the\nshort-name gate; INV-tapat/INV-maluk preserved). Admission criterion (from the\nWI-harin note as amended by WI-sozoj): real distinctive module namespace +\ntype-verified receiver + bounded method set. Add a `sqlalchemy.orm` /\n`sqlalchemy.engine` block to the same carve-out with a scoping comment.\n\n## Family\n\nSibling of WI-sozoj (done, Django), WI-sitos (Django instance-typing + transitive\nbases), WI-fuvuj (done, the `file` synthetic-module receiver-type precedent),\nWI-fabup (ambiguous_names for RESOLVED receivers). dispatch:F3 / WI-noham\nreceiver-resolution family."  # 44cb
